Claude DesktopGeneric MCP Client <p>Add the following to your <code>claude_desktop_config.json</code>:</p> <pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "ynab": {
      "command": "uvx",
      "args": ["you-need-an-advisor-mcp"],
      "env": {
        "YNAB_PAT": "your-personal-access-token"
      }
    }
  }
}
</code></pre> <p>Replace <code>your-personal-access-token</code> with the token from the installation step.</p> <p>See the Configuration page for file location details and additional options.</p> <p>Run the server with your token as an environment variable:</p> <pre><code>YNAB_PAT=your-personal-access-token uvx you-need-an-advisor-mcp
</code></pre> <p>Point your MCP client at the running server using its stdio transport.</p> New to MCP? <p>MCP clients connect to MCP servers over a standard protocol. Claude Desktop has built-in MCP support -- you just add the server configuration and it handles the rest. Other clients may require pointing at a running server process.</p> <p>Learn more about MCP | What is MCP?</p>
